# USE flags for the sway (real hardware) flavour on amd64.
#
# Currently unused: sway/amd64 is disabled in build-gentoo-stage4.yml. It
# exists so re-enabling that leg does not silently give x86 hardware the
# arm64 Mali drivers from package.use.hwaccel, which is what the previous
# arch-blind copy would have done.
#
#   x230  Intel Ivy Bridge, HD Graphics 4000 -> crocus
#
# crocus, not i965: mesa removed the i965 driver in 22.0, and crocus is what
# covers gen4 through gen7. iris only starts at gen8 (Broadwell), so it is
# wrong for this machine. The kernel side is already there -
# kernel-config-x230 has CONFIG_DRM_I915.
media-libs/mesa video_cards_crocus
